\DOC LOCAL_MUXPAIR_4_TAC

\TYPE {LOCAL_MUXPAIR_4_TAC : int -> string list -> tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Symbolically executes a block of machine code that conditionally swaps two
4-word field elements, advancing an {eventually} goal to a later machine state
and recording the two conditionally-selected results as new assumptions.

\DESCRIBE
{LOCAL_MUXPAIR_4_TAC n [s1;s2;s3;s4]} takes an {int} offset/index {n} selecting
which pair of destination slots the block writes (and correspondingly which
program point execution ends at), and a {string list} of four names used for
the newly introduced result variables and the source values they are defined
from. The goal has the form {A ?- eventually x86 (\s. ...) s_i}, where {A}
holds state-component assumptions about the current state variable {s_i}
together with pure arithmetic side conditions. The conclusion's state variable
is replaced by a later one, and the assumptions are rewritten: every assumption
mentioning the old state is discharged and re-added in the same form about the
new state, the pure arithmetic assumptions are retained (sometimes in a
different order), and further assumptions {z1 ... zp} are added giving the
updated program counter, the contents of the newly written destination blocks
as conditional expressions on the selector, defining equations for the freshly
named result variables, and an extended {MAYCHANGE} frame relating the initial
state to the new state; flag-read assumptions may also be introduced or carried
over.
{
   A ?- eventually x86 (\s. ...) s_i
   =================================================  LOCAL_MUXPAIR_4_TAC n [s1;s2;s3;s4]
   A[s_j/s_i], z1, ..., zp ?- eventually x86 (\s. ...) s_j
}

\COMMENTS
The observed traces show only this single kind of forward-stepping
transformation, on goals of this {eventually} form.

\ENDDOC
